{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## /rebar-debug Phase 2 — fix landed for review, and the `caused_by` attribution\n\n### Attribution: `fc20-2df1-426e-42ab` (Add administrative close dispositions)\n\nEstablished from the confirmed mechanism, by the protocol.\n\n**Blame the gate function's origin — and then reject it.** `close_plan_review_gate_check` was\nborn in `7cec0f64cf` (2026-07-22, ticket `2bbd-87f6-8765-4b00`, \"close: require current plan\nreview when configured\"). A `git log -S \"def close_plan_review_gate_check\"` over the file\nreturns **exactly that one commit** — the signature was never touched again before this change.\nSo there are **no intervening carriers** to walk through; the field narrows to two candidates.\n\n**The date test separates an omission from a later-created obligation.** On 2026-07-22 there was\nno obligation to omit. `superseded` / `obsolete` / `wontfix` did not exist as close classes at\nall, and `ADMINISTRATIVE_CLASSES` did not exist — both were introduced later, by the same commit\n(`git log -S` on each returns `9844f6de35` as their first appearance). The only dispositions\nthat existed were `duplicate` / `not_a_bug` / `escalated`, and they were scoped to **`bug`**\ntickets — which this gate **already exempts by type**. The trap was therefore **unreachable**\nwhen the gate was written: every link-backed disposition close of that era exited at the\nticket-type check. A gate cannot omit a case that cannot occur.\n\n**The obligation was created on 2026-08-14 by `9844f6de35` (ticket `fc20-2df1-426e-42ab`).**\nThat change extended administrative dispositions to `task` / `story` / `epic` — precisely the\nthree types the plan-review close gate is **not** exempt for — and so made the conflict reachable\nfor the first time. Its own file list is the decisive evidence: it modified\n`close_precheck.py` (+164) and `transition_close.py` (+29) — **both** close-gate call sites — and\ndid **not** touch `gates.py`. It taught the completion gate to honour the new evidence and left\nits sibling blind to it. That is the exact asymmetry Phase 1 measured at runtime.\n\nSo: **not** a defect in the gate's author's work, and **not** a policy decision anywhere. A\nlater change created a new obligation and discharged it on one of the two gates that owed it.\n`caused_by` = `fc20-2df1-426e-42ab`.\n\n### The fix\n\n`gates.close_plan_review_gate_check` takes keyword-only `close_class` / `tracker` (defaults keep\nall 8 existing callers — 2 production, 6 test — and the one string-literal `monkeypatch.setattr`\nreference unchanged). It exempts a close only when BOTH hold: the class is in the new\n`_LINK_BACKED_DISPOSITION_CLASSES = {\"duplicate\", \"superseded\"}`, AND\n`close_precheck._has_live_replacement_link(...)` — the completion gate's own predicate, reused\nrather than reimplemented, so the two gates cannot drift on what counts as evidence — returns\nTrue. `obsolete` / `wontfix` are deliberately excluded: reason-required, not link-backed, no\nverifiable evidence. Any unreadable tracker yields False, so the helper is fail-CLOSED.\n\nThe verdict is the distinct string `\"disposition\"`, never `\"exempt\"` — AC3. Both call sites in\n`transition_close.py` (the precheck and the locked `pre_status_check` recheck) thread the class,\nso the exemption cannot be granted at precheck and revoked under the write lock.\n\n### RED -> GREEN -> mutation\n\nRED first, and for the reported reason verbatim:\n\n```\nE       AssertionError: assert 1 == 0\nE        +  where 1 = _close('64ea-2c99-19c0-4d18', '--class=superseded')\n--- Captured stderr call ---\nplan-review close gate: unsigned: no certified plan-review attestation. Run rebar\nreview-plan 64ea-2c99-19c0-4d18 separately, then retry close.\n```\n\n7 failed / 2 passed before the fix (the 2 assert unchanged behaviour and are green either way);\n9 passed after.\n\n**Mutation check** — the suite is not a tautology. Re-seeding the exact defect returns it to RED\nboth ways:\n\n| seeded defect | result |\n|---|---|\n| drop the live-link condition (exempt on class alone) | 2 failed — the two anti-bypass tests |\n| widen the set to `obsolete` / `wontfix` | 2 failed — both scope tests |\n\n### Gates\n\n`make lint` clean; `make typecheck` clean (598 files); complexity ratchet\n`active=49 new=0 increased=0 stale=0` — no baseline bump, the branch was extracted into\n`_disposition_close_exempt` along the existing seam. The inherited caller sweep passes\n(118 tests across the 4 close-gate/disposition suites), plus 1082 in a broader\nclose/transition/gate sweep and 203 docs tests."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787256990506053001,"uuid":"1151138b-abd8-489f-acc2-235d2f0dd7a2"}